    "questions": {
      "route": {
        "criteria": {
          "hold": "Do not dispatch now; wait for pressure to ease. When the local lane is not admitting (full, paused or unavailable), well-defined, routine or deferrable work should usually hold for it rather than spend a pressed metered lane. On a sliding scale, hard, high-risk or urgent work may still take the metered lane; weigh expected wait against urgency without a numeric threshold. When exactly one lane can serve the node, a hold waits for that lane alone, as hold_waits_for states.",
          "local:deepseek-v4.1-flash:clive": {
            "backend": "clive",
            "effort": "high",
